@startuml
' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
' '   description:  16+ action distributed workflow with fork/join, call-behavior, signals, and exception flow.
'   usecase:      Teach call-behavior (rake), send-signal/accept-event, multiple decisions, exception handling.
'   complexity:   complex
'   domain:       distributed-systems
' ============================================================================
title Example Activity - Complex Distributed Workflow

start

:Receive service request;
:Authenticate caller;

' First DECISION — guard the whole pipeline on authorization.
if (Authorized?) then (yes)
else (no)
  :Return 401 Unauthorized;
  ' EXCEPTION FLOW: an abnormal exit path. UML models this as a dedicated
  ' exception edge from a node to a handler; here it terminates early.
  stop
endif

:Parse request payload;
:Validate schema;

' CALL-BEHAVIOR node (shown with a "rake" glyph in full UML): an action that
' itself invokes another, nested activity diagram. The rake indicates
' "this box is elaborated in its own activity elsewhere."
:Run risk assessment;
note right
  <<call-behavior>>
  Invokes nested activity:
  "RiskAssessment" (rake glyph).
  See: risk-assessment.puml
end note

' FORK into three concurrent enrichment flows.
fork
  :Enrich data via Service A;
fork again
  :Enrich data via Service B;
fork again
  :Fetch user profile;
end fork

' SEND-SIGNAL node: the activity emits an asynchronous signal to another process.
' (PlantUML has no native signal glyph; we annotate an action to convey it.)
:Publish "OrderPending" event;
note right: <<send-signal>>\nemits to message bus

' ACCEPT-EVENT node: the activity WAITS for an incoming signal before continuing.
:Wait for inventory confirmation;
note right: <<accept-event>>\nblocks until signal arrives

' Multiple chained DECISION points.
if (Inventory confirmed?) then (yes)
  if (All enrichments ready?) then (yes)
    :Compose full response;
    :Persist result;
    :Publish "OrderConfirmed" event;
    note right: <<send-signal>>
  else (timeout)
    :Compose partial response;
    :Log timeout warning;
  endif
else (no)
  :Compensate prior steps;
  :Publish "OrderFailed" event;
  note right: <<send-signal>>
endif

' A guaranteed final step that executes on both the success and exception paths.
:Record audit trail;
stop

' TEACHING NOTES:
'   - A call-behavior node is reusable: change the nested activity once,
'     every caller benefits.
'   - Send-signal / accept-event pairs model asynchronous hand-offs between
'     independent activities or processes.
'   - Exception flow should still run cleanup (compensation) before terminating.
'   - Forks can have more than two concurrent branches (here: three).
@enduml
